INT. ABANDONED BOWLING ALLEY - LANE NINE - NIGHT

Neon pins flicker over a taped-off lane. Underground curling, bowling stones on waxed lanes. Cash piles on the ball return.

COACH ODALYS BRANCH (50s, ex-champion, cane) leans on the scorer's table. HIRO TANABE (20s, wiry, wrapped wrists) chalks his hands. His rival, DESMOND "DEZ" OYELARAN (20s, broad, grinning) stretches at the foul line. BIG PAT (60s, bookie, cardigan) counts money. LUCIA FERRARI (30s, referee, whistle on a bootlace) holds the stopwatch.

LUCIA
Final frame. Hiro needs a strike. Dez needs a spare.

HIRO
I know what I need.

COACH BRANCH
Eyes on the headpin, not on him.

DEZ
He can look at me all he wants. He gave his uncle the same look before he lost.

HIRO
Say that again.

DEZ
Your uncle. Lost his house on this lane.

COACH BRANCH
Hiro, he is feeding you. Don't eat.

BIG PAT
Nobody is eating. Everybody is betting. Eat on your own time.

LUCIA
Sixty seconds, Hiro.

HIRO
Coach, he stood there when my uncle signed the paper. He smiled at him.

COACH BRANCH
Then he's smiling now because he's scared. He's scared, so he talks. You hear me?

DEZ
I'm scared of nothing in this building.

BIG PAT
Then you won't mind me doubling your side.

DEZ
Double it.

LUCIA
Pat, you can't change the stake mid-frame.

BIG PAT
I can change anything I like. It's my money, my lane, my building.

COACH BRANCH
It's the bank's building.

BIG PAT
The bank's cousin's building. Close enough.

HIRO
Lucia, start the clock.

LUCIA
You sure?

HIRO
He told me to wait for him last time. I waited. Start it.

COACH BRANCH
Then he walks the approach slow. Four steps. No fifth.

HIRO
Four. No fifth.

DEZ
He always takes a fifth.

COACH BRANCH
Not tonight.

LUCIA
Clock's running. Fifty.

BIG PAT
Everyone breathe.

HIRO
Dez.

DEZ
What.

HIRO
When I hit this, give my uncle the deed back.

DEZ
When you hit it.

LUCIA
Forty.

COACH BRANCH
Go.
